# A callable merge's model whose only line is its trailer `return:` (T7-TRAILER-ONLY-MODEL-CRASH: the
# translator crashed on it).  r reads k, a field of the unit.  make, whose own k is 50, returns merge(r): the
# node walks r's trailer alone and reads k in the copy of the unit made at the merge.  prep wrote 9 before
# the merge; bump writes 11 after it.  w's copy reads 9 before and after bump; the original r, called by orig
# after bump, reads 11.  The root calls are above the unit's declaration of k: no caller binding reaches them.
# The same program with r's return indented is unit_t7_trailer_only_copy_indented.  Entry 7.
int: z0 prep()
@: w make()
int: c1 (plain())
int: z1 bump()
int: c2 (plain())
int: o (orig())
int: k 9

fn: r () int
return: k

fn: make () fn: () int
    int: k 50
    return: merge(r)

fn: plain () int
    return: w()
end: plain

fn: orig () int
    return: r()
end: orig

fn: prep () int
    node\k: 9
    return: 0
end: prep

fn: bump () int
    node\k: 11
    return: 0
end: bump

int: ok 81
if: c1 = 9 && c2 = 9 && o = 11
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
